From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DwUsbHostDxe: bound the deferred transfer timeout

DwHcAsyncInterruptTransfer stamps every deferred request with a one
second timeout. That number is not a transfer budget, it is a TPL hold
time: DwHcPeriodicHandler is an EVT_TIMER | EVT_NOTIFY_SIGNAL event
registered at TPL_NOTIFY with a one millisecond period, and for each due
request it calls DwHcDeferredTransfer, which arms a timer for
Req->TimeOut milliseconds and then runs DwHcTransfer synchronously.
DwHcTransfer raises to TPL_NOTIFY itself and spins in Wait4Chhltd. So
one endpoint that stops halting its channel can hold TPL_NOTIFY for a
full second, and nothing at TPL_CALLBACK or TPL_APPLICATION runs for
the duration.

That went unnoticed while the only deferred endpoints on this platform
belonged to a keyboard or a mouse, which sit idle and NAK promptly --
Wait4Chhltd returns XFER_NAK, DwHcTransfer breaks out, and
DwHcDeferredTransfer swallows the NAK without ever approaching the
timeout. A CDC-NCM NIC changed that. Its notification endpoint is polled
on the same deferred list, the link carries real traffic, and the paths
that do reach the timeout -- XFER_NOT_HALTED from Wait4Bit, and the
XFER_CSPLIT and XFER_FRMOVRUN retry loops -- became reachable in
practice. EfiBootManagerConnectAll runs at TPL_APPLICATION, and its
progress went to a crawl: DEBUG output was visibly cut mid-string by
notify-level work, which is starvation rather than slow work.

Only interrupt endpoints are ever placed on the deferred list -- EpType
is set to DWC2_HCCHAR_EPTYPE_INTR a few lines above -- and an interrupt
transaction is a single short packet. Five milliseconds is three orders
of magnitude more than one needs and still bounds the worst case at
something BDS can absorb. A transaction that has not halted by then is
not going to.

Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
@@ -1246,7 +1246,18 @@
   NewReq->IgnoreAck = FALSE;
   NewReq->CallbackFunction = CallbackFunction;
   NewReq->CallbackContext = Context;
-  NewReq->TimeOut = 1000; /* 1000 ms */
+  /*
+   * DwHcPeriodicHandler runs at TPL_NOTIFY once a millisecond and calls
+   * DwHcDeferredTransfer synchronously, so this value is the longest the
+   * driver can hold TPL_NOTIFY in a single tick -- and nothing at
+   * TPL_CALLBACK or below runs while it does. A second was survivable
+   * while the only deferred endpoints belonged to idle keyboards; once a
+   * CDC-NCM NIC started polling here it was enough to starve BDS. Only
+   * interrupt endpoints are deferred, and their transactions are a single
+   * short packet, so one that has not halted in five milliseconds is not
+   * going to.
+   */
+  NewReq->TimeOut = 5; /* ms */
 
   InsertTailList (&DwHc->DeferredList, &NewReq->List);
   Status = EFI_SUCCESS;
